latest&quot;&gt;https://github.com/speed47/dvdisaster/releases/tag/latest&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Which asset should I download?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you&#39;re using Windows, get the &lt;code&gt;win32-portable.zip&lt;/code&gt; version&lt;br&gt;
If you&#39;re using any flavor of Linux (Ubuntu, CentOS, Arch, OpenSUSE, etc.), get the &lt;code&gt;AppImage&lt;/code&gt; version, it doesn&#39;t need installation&lt;br&gt;
If you&#39;re using macOS, get the &lt;code&gt;dmg&lt;/code&gt; file, and read the warning below&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Warning for macOS users&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you&#39;re getting the &lt;code&gt;dvdisaster.app is damaged and can&#39;t be opened&lt;/code&gt; error message when attempting to launch dvdisaster, you have to run the following command first:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;highlight highlight-source-shell notranslate position-relative overflow-auto&quot; data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=&quot;sudo xattr -c /Applications/dvdisaster.app&quot;&gt;&lt;pre&gt;sudo xattr -c /Applications/dvdisaster.app&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is only needed once, then, you should then be able to use the program. More information about this can be found here: &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;2114261103&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/speed47/dvdisaster/issues/85&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;issue&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/speed47/dvdisaster/issues/85/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/speed47/dvdisaster/issues/85&quot;&gt;#85&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
